  "transport_events_result": "5 of 6 grew; validator-1 did not, as expected for the proposer",
  "validator_1_not_grown": {
   "cause": "validator-1 was the view-0 proposer. The round ran as a separate CLI process that signs the proposer's own vote in-process (crates/node/src/transport_runtime.rs:3066) and connects only to the other five validators' transport-validator-serve, so validator-1's serve process received no connection and wrote no event",
   "fd": "fd 3 still points at the live path, same inode (1071149), flags 02102001 (O_APPEND); fdinfo pos is the pre-truncation offset 13867827262, which O_APPEND ignores",
   "journal": "journalctl -u postfiat-validator-1.service since 2026-09-29 12:00: no entries",
   "stderr_log": "unchanged since 2026-09-28 07:40Z; no event-log error",
   "confirmation_owed": "the next block validator-1 does not propose (1064 goes to validator-2 at view 0) should write to its file; not done here, only one grant was authorized"
  },
  "rpc_events": {
   "decision": "rule added",
   "why": "rpc_serve_inner opens --event-log once with open_transport_event_log (create+append) and holds it for the process lifetime (crates/node/src/rpc_serve_runtime.rs:43-47); write_rpc_serve_event_or_degrade sets event_log_writable=false and degraded only when a write or flush fails (crates/node/src/rpc_cli.rs:655-674); the flag never reads the file's size or content, request_index is an in-memory counter, and nothing in crates/node reads the file (only tests). Observed RPC fd 4 flags 02102001 (O_APPEND) on all six",
   "rule_path": "/etc/logrotate.d/postfiat-rpc-events",
   "rule_text": "/var/log/postfiat/validator-*/rpc-events.ndjson {\n    size 512M\n    rotate 3\n    compress\n    delaycompress\n    missingok\n    notifempty\n    copytruncate\n}\n",
   "rule_sha256": "a48c714e142d0e94ca054f35751e8ec18ec6b70e9acd8224d7e6feb17132b9a3",
   "rule_mode": "root:root 0644",
